                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`board install <runtime> --dry-run` prints a unified diff of proposed config changes, and `planJson` re-serializes the whole config so pre-existing lines commonly count as changed (compact single-line configs reflow entirely; pretty-printed files rewrite the former last key's line with a trailing comma). The only redaction on those lines is `safeDiffLine`: a key-name denylist (token|secret|password|credential|private_key|access_key|api_key|authorization) plus URL-userinfo scrubbing. A secret stored under any other key name (for example `openai_key`) is emitted verbatim to stdout inside the diff, violating the backlog 117 #8 claim that the installer never echoes credentials into diffs. Reproduced end-to-end through the real CLI stdout with an invented marker secret; the denylisted-key negative control is correctly redacted."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "b67ea6a75e8e5f59:1",
            "security/v1": "security/v1:sha256:38925fe3650e7b6455a6bdb228fa17c3b884038260bcdf90223b094aac4d68f9"
