                  "startLine": 362
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "deliverOpenCodeMentions (new in this change set) resolves wake targets by calling listPresence without a limit, so it examines at most the first 200 presence keys of the untrusted shared store in lexicographic order (DEFAULT_WHO_LIMIT in committed packages/presence, out of diff scope) and stops. Any store writer can cheaply create 200 structurally valid heartbeat records under a low-sorting name; the victim's record is then never examined and the wake silently never fires (errors are discarded by Promise.allSettled and nothing logs). Validated end-to-end through the real sink: 1 wake POST without flood, 0 POSTs with exactly 200 flood records. Availability-only: wake endpoints still derive solely from the local owner-only session registry, so integrity and confidentiality are unaffected."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "e724a9b5b8347723:1",
            "security/v1": "security/v1:sha256:19696a290f68816da992b2579af6adc10d57002189598f82b0d526f7dc4eb80e"
          },
